---
interface Props {
  category: string;
}

const { category } = Astro.props;
const cat = (category || 'general').toLowerCase().replace(/\s+/g, '-');
---

{cat === 'finance' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Core Financial Calculation Frameworks
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Making informed personal finance decisions requires understanding how interest, compounding, and repayment schedules work mathematically. Below is an overview of the foundational models used across our financial tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📊</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Reducing-Balance Amortization</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Most home loans, personal loans, and vehicle financing follow a reducing-balance method. Each Equated Monthly Installment (EMI) consists of an interest portion and a principal portion. In the early stages of a loan, interest comprises the majority of each payment; as the outstanding principal decreases, the principal component increases exponentially.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📈</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Compounding & Time Value of Money</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Systematic Investment Plans (SIP) and compound interest tools utilize periodic reinvestment of earnings. Because compounding accelerates geometrically over long horizons, small incremental contributions made early in an investment lifecycle generate significantly larger wealth multiples than larger lump sums invested later.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📉</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Inflation-Adjusted Real Returns</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Nominal returns can create an illusion of rapid growth. To calculate genuine purchasing power growth, investors evaluate real returns using the formula: <span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">Real Rate = ((1 + Nominal) / (1 + Inflation)) - 1</span>. Always evaluate your retirement corpus and long-term savings against expected annual inflation rates.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/60 p-6 dark:border-amber-900/40 dark:bg-amber-950/20 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⚠️</span> Important Financial Disclaimer
        </div>
        <p>
          Calculations provided across our financial tools are for informational and planning purposes only. They use standard mathematical formulas and statutory tax slabs as published by authoritative regulatory bodies. Actual loan terms, processing fees, interest recalculations, and tax obligations vary by lending institution, jurisdiction, and individual circumstances. Consult a certified financial planner or chartered accountant before executing major borrowing or investment commitments.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'construction' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Civil Engineering Estimation & Material Thumb Rules
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Accurate quantity surveying and Bill of Quantities (BOQ) preparation prevent material shortages and budget overruns on construction projects. Below are the verified empirical factors and Indian Standard (IS 456 / CPWD) guidelines embedded in our calculators.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🧱</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Dry-to-Wet Volume Factor (1.54)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            When dry ingredients (cement, sand, aggregate) are mixed with water, air voids between the particles collapse, causing a volume reduction of approximately 30% to 35%. To produce 1 m³ of compacted wet concrete, engineers must procure approximately <strong>1.54 m³</strong> of dry materials. For mortar and plaster, a factor of 1.30 to 1.33 is typically applied.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🏗️</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Steel Reinforcement Thumb Rules</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Preliminary steel requirement can be estimated from structural concrete volume using established CPWD thumb rules:
            <br />• <strong>Slabs:</strong> 0.7% to 1.0% (~70–80 kg/m³)
            <br />• <strong>Beams:</strong> 1.0% to 2.0% (~100–150 kg/m³)
            <br />• <strong>Columns:</strong> 1.5% to 3.0% (~150–250 kg/m³)
            <br />• <strong>Footings:</strong> 0.5% to 0.8% (~50–70 kg/m³)
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📐</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Nominal Concrete Mix Proportions</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Per IS 456:2000 specifications for nominal mixes (Cement : Sand : Coarse Aggregate by volume):
            <br />• <strong>M10:</strong> 1 : 3 : 6 (PCC / lean foundation base)
            <br />• <strong>M15:</strong> 1 : 2 : 4 (plain mass concrete, flooring)
            <br />• <strong>M20:</strong> 1 : 1.5 : 3 (standard RCC slabs, beams, columns)
            <br />• <strong>M25:</strong> 1 : 1 : 2 (heavy structural components)
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-amber-200 bg-amber-50/60 p-6 dark:border-amber-900/40 dark:bg-amber-950/20 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-amber-900 dark:text-amber-300 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>⚠️</span> Civil Engineering Disclaimer
        </div>
        <p>
          Calculations generated by these tools provide preliminary estimates for budgeting, planning, and ordering material batches. Always account for 5% to 10% on-site handling, cutting, and overlap wastage. Structural design and load-bearing construction must be certified by a licensed structural engineer following local municipal bylaws and structural codes.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'health' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Scientific Biometric Equations & Nutritional Metrics
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Anthropometric measurements provide useful benchmarks when planning caloric targets, evaluating body composition, and tracking fitness progress. Our calculators implement peer-reviewed equations recognized by international health organizations.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🔥</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Basal Metabolic Rate (BMR)</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            BMR represents the baseline energy expended to maintain vital involuntary functions (respiration, circulation, cellular repair) at complete rest. Our tools implement the <strong>Mifflin-St Jeor equation</strong>, established in clinical studies as the most accurate predictor of resting metabolic rate in non-athletic and general adult populations.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">⚖️</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Body Mass Index (BMI) & Limitations</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            BMI evaluates weight relative to height squared (<span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">kg/m²</span>) using WHO thresholds (Underweight &lt;18.5, Normal 18.5–24.9, Overweight 25.0–29.9, Obese ≥30.0). Note that BMI is a population screening metric; it does not distinguish between lean skeletal muscle mass, bone density, and adipose tissue.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🥗</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">TDEE & Macronutrient Distribution</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Total Daily Energy Expenditure (TDEE) adjusts BMR by Physical Activity Level (PAL) multipliers (1.2 for sedentary up to 1.9 for extreme athletic regimens). Sustainable weight management generally targets a moderate deficit of 300–500 kcal/day for fat loss, or a controlled surplus for hypertrophic muscle gain.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-rose-200 bg-rose-50/60 p-6 dark:border-rose-900/40 dark:bg-rose-950/20 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-rose-900 dark:text-rose-300 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🩺</span> Medical & Health Disclaimer
        </div>
        <p>
          The health, caloric, and fitness calculators on this website are provided strictly for informational, educational, and general reference purposes. They do not constitute personalized medical advice, diagnosis, or clinical treatment plans. Individuals with metabolic conditions, eating disorders, cardiovascular risk factors, or pregnancy should consult a qualified physician or registered dietitian before modifying dietary intake or exercise routines.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'math' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Mathematical Precision & Numerical Methods
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Our mathematical calculators are engineered for academic rigor, scientific inquiry, and engineering problem-solving. Below are the numerical principles and rounding standards applied across our mathematical tools.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🔢</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">IEEE 754 Floating-Point Precision</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Computations execute client-side using 64-bit double-precision floating-point arithmetic conforming to IEEE 754 standards (providing 53 bits of precision or approximately 15–17 significant decimal digits). For financial and sensitive percentages, epsilon-aware clamping is employed to prevent binary rounding artifacts.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📊</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Descriptive Statistics & Dispersion</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Our statistical tools differentiate between sample statistics (degrees of freedom <span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">n - 1</span> using Bessel's correction) and full population parameters (<span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">N</span>). Mean, median, standard deviation, and variance are computed using single-pass numerically stable algorithms.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📐</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Scientific & Trigonometric Functions</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Trigonometric functions support both radian and degree modes with explicit conversion constants (<span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">π / 180</span>). Advanced functions including logarithms (natural base <span class="font-mono text-slate-800 dark:text-slate-200">e</span> and base 10), permutations, combinations, and matrix determinants follow standard algebraic identities.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-blue-200 bg-blue-50/60 p-6 dark:border-blue-900/40 dark:bg-blue-950/20 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-blue-900 dark:text-blue-300 flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>💡</span> Academic & Computational Verification
        </div>
        <p>
          Each calculation is accompanied by formulas and step-by-step mathematical reasoning to support classroom learning and engineering peer-review. For mission-critical aerospace, structural, or cryptographic applications, verify results against formal computational algebra packages (e.g. Mathematica, SymPy, or certified lab instruments).
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'compiler-tools' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          In-Browser Execution & WebAssembly Runtimes
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Our online compilers and code editors allow programmers, students, and engineers to test algorithms without installing local SDKs or heavyweight development environments. Below is how our sandboxed execution architecture works.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">⚡</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Client-Side Sandboxing</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Code execution leverages modern browser technologies including WebAssembly (Wasm) and sandboxed JavaScript workers. Python scripts execute via Pyodide Wasm, SQL statements run via in-memory SQLite (sql.js), and JavaScript executes directly inside an isolated worker. This eliminates server queue delays and delivers instantaneous output.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🔒</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Strict Privacy & Zero Server Uploads</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Because execution occurs inside your browser session, your source code, proprietary algorithms, database schemas, and input data are never transmitted to backend servers or logged into external databases. Your intellectual property remains strictly confined to your device.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">⏱️</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Realistic Browser Constraints</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Browser sandboxing protects your device by prohibiting unrestricted low-level OS file system operations, raw TCP sockets, and kernel calls. To prevent accidental browser freezing caused by infinite loops, execution tasks enforce an automatic timeout mechanism.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🛠️</span> Educational & Prototyping Focus
        </div>
        <p>
          These online programming tools are built for algorithmic practice, interview preparation, debugging code snippets, and learning computer science concepts. For full production compilation with external package managers (such as pip, npm, or NuGet), native containerized or local compiler environments are recommended.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'image-tools' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Client-Side Canvas Processing & Image Optimization
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Our image utilities perform resizing, compression, cropping, and color manipulation without uploading files to cloud storage. Below is how our in-browser graphic processing pipeline protects your privacy.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🎨</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">HTML5 Canvas & Pixel Manipulation</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Image transformations (resizing, aspect ratio clamping, grayscale, color inversion, blur filtering) operate directly on pixel arrays via the HTML5 2D Canvas API. Image buffers exist in temporary browser memory and are discarded immediately upon session closure.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📦</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Lossy vs Lossless Compression</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Our compression algorithms provide granular quality sliders. Modern WebP and JPEG compression leverage discrete cosine transform (DCT) quantization for dramatic bandwidth reduction, while PNG maintains lossless deflate encoding to preserve crisp vector edges and transparent alpha channels.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🛡️</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Zero Server Ingestion Guarantee</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Unlike traditional online file converters that upload user photos to remote third-party servers, all conversions occur locally on your machine via JavaScript FileReader and Blob APIs. Sensitive personal, identity, and proprietary graphics never leave your device.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>💡</span> Performance Optimization Tip
        </div>
        <p>
          For optimal web performance, convert legacy PNG and JPG assets to modern WebP format. WebP typically achieves 25% to 35% smaller file sizes at visually identical quality levels, improving Google Core Web Vitals (Largest Contentful Paint) across mobile devices.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
)}

{cat === 'pdf-tools' && (
  <section class="border-t border-slate-200 bg-white px-4 py-12 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-900/60 sm:py-16">
    <div class="mx-auto max-w-7xl space-y-10">
      <div class="max-w-3xl space-y-3">
        <h2 class="text-2xl font-black tracking-tight text-slate-900 dark:text-white sm:text-3xl">
          Client-Side PDF Manipulation & Cryptographic Security
        </h2>
        <p class="text-sm leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-300">
          Working with contracts, invoices, and sensitive legal documentation requires absolute data discretion. Our browser-based PDF suite merges, splits, compresses, and extracts pages without transmitting records across public networks.
        </p>
      </div>

      <div class="grid gap-8 md:grid-cols-3">
        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">📑</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">PDF Binary Stream Parsing</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            PDF manipulation utilizes modern WebAssembly and JavaScript binary stream parsers (such as pdf-lib). Operations like merging multiple documents, deleting pages, or rearranging sheet sequences modify the underlying cross-reference tables (XRef) entirely in browser memory.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">🔐</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Zero Cloud Ingestion Compliance</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Most online PDF tools upload your sensitive tax forms, medical records, or corporate NDAs to remote cloud servers for conversion. In contrast, our tools run 100% locally on your device, ensuring complete adherence to GDPR and data sovereignty best practices.
          </p>
        </div>

        <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/70 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/50 space-y-3">
          <div class="text-2xl">⚡</div>
          <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white">Sub-Second Processing</h3>
          <p class="text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-600 dark:text-slate-400">
            Because operations do not incur upload or download network latency, file processing takes milliseconds rather than minutes. Output files download immediately as fresh binary Blobs without server queues or rate-limiting subscriptions.
          </p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="rounded-2xl border border-slate-200 bg-slate-50/80 p-6 dark:border-slate-800 dark:bg-slate-950/40 text-xs leading-relaxed text-slate-700 dark:text-slate-300 space-y-2">
        <div class="font-bold text-slate-900 dark:text-white flex items-center gap-2">
          <span>🔒</span> Document Security Recommendation
        </div>
        <p>
          Always ensure confidential PDF documents are password-protected before sharing via email. For digitally signed PDFs, note that rearranging or removing pages invalidates existing cryptographic certificates, which require re-signing after structural edits.
